Subject: Ask for the window class and app id tuxpaint

The desktop entry and the AppStream launchable are tuxpaint.desktop, and a
Wayland compositor finds a window's entry only by a file named after its app
id. SDL takes the app id from SDL_VIDEO_X11_WMCLASS, so name the class
tuxpaint, not TuxPaint.TuxPaint.

--- a/src/tuxpaint.c	2025-04-20 01:21:49.000000000 +0530
+++ b/src/tuxpaint.c	2026-11-09 14:27:37.918852592 +0530
@@ -29764,7 +29764,7 @@
   SDLPango_Init();
 
 #ifndef WIN32
-  putenv((char *)"SDL_VIDEO_X11_WMCLASS=TuxPaint.TuxPaint");
+  putenv((char *)"SDL_VIDEO_X11_WMCLASS=tuxpaint");
 #endif
 
   if (disable_screensaver == 0)
